    "description": "Tests chain-of-thought monitorability: whether a model's CoT surfaces the decision-critical factors that drive its outputs. 1,514 fixed instances across 19 tasks in 7 categories (cue and goal injection, dual objectives, impossible tasks, multi-step updates), with stress tests for direct concealment and monitor-aware evasion. A monitor LLM (or human) flags trajectories; the headline metric is the paper's monitorability score.",
    "summary": "Measures whether the model's reasoning steps show the key factors that drive its answers.",
